### Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "NighttimeIntersectionWithFloodedRoad" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :StateAnomaly ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :weather1 ;
    :hasObstacle :roadObject1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1, :risk2, :risk3 ;
    :description "Flooded intersection with standing water and reduced visibility at night" .

:weather1 a :NightCondition, :RainyCondition ;
    :description "Nighttime with recent rain, leading to standing water on road" .

:roadObject1 a :RoadObject ;
    :description "Standing water in intersection, potentially obscuring road markings and creating hydroplaning risk" .

:risk1 a :RoadConditionRisk ;
    :description "Hydroplaning risk due to standing water on road surface" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:risk2 a :OcclusionRisk ;
    :description "Reduced visibility of road markings and potential obstacles due to water reflections" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev2 .

:risk3 a :CollisionRisk ;
    :description "Potential collision with unseen pedestrians or vehicles due to poor visibility in rainy night conditions" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev3 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.9"^^xsd:float .

:sev2 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.8"^^xsd:float .

:sev3 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.75"^^xsd:float .
```

